# Indirection: Names Written in Text

FileMaker stores a direct reference (a field in a calculation, the script of a Perform Script step) by its internal ID, and updates it when the target is renamed. A **name written in text** is not updated: `GetField ( "Invoice::Total" )`, `Set Field By Name [ $target ]`, `Perform Script [ By name: $callback ]`, `Go to Object [ "btnSave" ]`, the table and column names in an `ExecuteSQL` query.

This report lists every such place found in **{{ source_file }}**: {{ r.total }} in all. Before you rename something, check its page: the **Referenced by Name** section lists what would break.

